A school pupil criticises her municipality's building project in an online post – she does not have to fear arrest. {{1}}
All children in a village can attend primary school free of charge, regardless of how much their parents earn. {{2}}
A suspect must not be beaten during questioning – even if the police want a confession. {{3}}
In court, the same rules apply to the mayor's daughter as to everyone else. {{4}}
The state must not kill anyone arbitrarily – executions without any form of trial violate this right. {{5}}
A journalist publishes an investigation exposing uncomfortable facts about a public authority and is not punished for it. {{6}}
Even people living in a poor region should be able to learn to read and write. {{7}}
No one may be subjected to degrading treatment in prison. {{8}}
A new law applies equally to rich and poor people. {{9}}
Emergency services must help people whose lives are in danger – whoever they are. {{10}}
